└── MQTT client for publishing telemetry to a broker
    ├── Candidates : paho-mqtt, gmqtt, amqtt, aiomqtt
    ├── Used APIs  : Client, connect, publish
    ├── Pitfalls   : paho-mqtt is synchronous (blocking connect/publish); aiomqtt, gmqtt, and amqtt are asyncio-based and require an event loop and async/await
    │   throughout the calling code; aiomqtt uses an async context manager (`async with Client(...) as client`) instead of explicit connect()/publish() calls; 
    │   Return value semantics differ: paho's publish() returns a MQTTMessageInfo with `.rc` (used here via getattr), while async clients typically return None
    │   or raise exceptions on failure instead of encoding an rc code; client_id and connection parameters (host, port, qos) are passed differently across 
    │   these libraries and may require config-layer changes; amqtt's API has diverged significantly across versions and its maintenance status is less stable 
    │   than paho-mqtt
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── paho.mqtt.client.Client is used synchronously to connect to a broker and publish messages with QoS. gmqtt, amqtt, and aiomqtt are all MQTT client 
        libraries that could serve the same broker-publishing role, though they use async/await and context-manager based APIs rather than paho's synchronous 
        callback-based model.

