│    30 def _gmqtt_threadsafe_publish_wrapper(client, loop, topic, payload, qos: int = 0):                                                                    │
│    31     """Publish through gmqtt from the *event loop's* thread, not the caller's.                                                                        │
│    32                                                                                                                                                       │
│    33     paho-mqtt's `Client.publish()` is safe to call from any thread and                                                                                │
│    34     returns an `MQTTMessageInfo` whose `.rc` is `MQTT_ERR_SUCCESS` (0) when                                                                           │
│    35     the packet was queued, or `MQTT_ERR_NO_CONN` (4) -- without raising --                                                                            │
│    36     when the client is not currently connected to a broker; the message is                                                                            │
│    37     just dropped in that case. gmqtt's `Client.publish()` touches asyncio                                                                             │
│    38     transport/state that belongs to the background event loop, so it must                                                                             │
│    39     not be invoked directly from the caller's thread; instead we marshal it                                                                           │
│    40     onto the loop via `run_coroutine_threadsafe(...).result()`, which blocks                                                                          │
│    41     the caller until gmqtt has actually processed the call (not merely                                                                                │
│    42     scheduled it) and re-raises whatever gmqtt raised.                                                                                                │
│    43                                                                                                                                                       │
│    44     gmqtt itself returns nothing from `publish()` -- it does not hand back a                                                                          │
│    45     status code, so on success there is nothing to "use"; we report rc=0 to                                                                           │
│    46     mean "the library accepted and queued the message" (paho's                                                                                        │
│    47     MQTT_ERR_SUCCESS for that same case), not "the broker confirmed                                                                                   │
│    48     delivery". The one failure gmqtt reports for the same condition paho                                                                              │
│    49     reports MQTT_ERR_NO_CONN for -- no live connection to publish on -- it                                                                            │
│    50     reports by raising (its transport is `None` or closed), so we catch                                                                               │
│    51     exactly that family of transport failures and translate it into the                                                                               │
